& [Phase0Baseline] is preserve and measure the starting state
  + [inputs] is canonical specification, exploded requirement set, existing eight CoreAcceptance fixtures, and passed llama.cpp seam probe
  + [actions] is record toolchain versions, establish Cargo workspace layout, add fixture corpus paths, and create test command surface
  + [proof] is clean build skeleton and reproducible test invocation
  + [exit] is slice_1 can add machine forms without revisiting repository identity

& [Phase1CoreIR] is implement CEB-001 through CEB-003
  + [actions] is define versioned semantic IR, transition records, proof records, fault records, and eight fixture encodings
  + [actions] is implement deterministic evaluator skeleton sufficient only for CoreAcceptance
  + [proof] is all eight fixtures expose before state, decision, after state, trace, proof, and fault
  + [checkpoint] is review type boundaries before trusted-package work
  + [exit] is machine forms are stable enough to serialize and hash

& [Phase2TrustedPackage] is implement CEB-004 through CEB-006
  + [depends_on] is Phase1CoreIR
  + [actions] is define fixture compiler or loader, canonical serialization, digests, test signer, recognition certificate, scope checks, and lifecycle checks
  + [actions] is compile one bounded SOP package with semantic addresses and exact source spans
  + [proof] is valid package admission plus unsigned, modified, corrupted, stale, revoked, mixed, downgraded, and scope-invalid rejection
  + [proof] is line relocation followed by recompilation preserves semantic identity while display locators change
  + [exit] is queries can consume only admitted package authority

& [Phase3DeterministicQuery] is implement CEB-007 through CEB-010
  + [depends_on] is Phase1CoreIR and Phase2TrustedPackage
  + [actions] is implement request validation, exact lookup, contextual filtering, typed traversal, boundary accounting, quote recovery, proof assembly, and budgets
  + [actions] is add lexical association only as a distinguishable derived candidate path
  + [proof] is typed detail fixtures, ambiguity fixtures, exclusion fixtures, relation-path fixtures, digest-verified quote fixtures, and visible fault fixtures
  + [baseline] is capture correctness, recall, latency, memory, result size, and proof-completeness data
  + [exit] is direct-core query protocol and normalized result digest are stable

& [Phase4CLI] is implement CEB-011 through CEB-013
  + [depends_on] is Phase3DeterministicQuery
  + [actions] is implement versioned JSON request on stdin or explicit file, machine-only stdout, diagnostic stderr, stable exit classes, inspect command, and query command
  + [proof] is golden protocol fixtures, malformed input faults, package faults, budget faults, and direct-core semantic equivalence
  + [Codex_use] is Codex may invoke the local CLI as a bounded read-only inference coprocessor through the documented subprocess contract
  + [exit] is repeated subprocess calls are deterministic and operationally adequate

& [Phase5CodexMCP] is implement CEB-014 and CEB-015
